DCC - forked into devsys on 2026-10-02 from ~/projects/dcc/CoCoC
(Source/Compiler/{CPP,CC09,COpt,DCC}): commit 68fdbf9 plus the owner's
uncommitted changes in that working tree, saved as uncommitted-at-fork.patch
(CPP dues.c/lex.c/parse.c, COpt inst.c/labels.c/optim.c, CC09/GNUmakefile,
DCC/dcc.c). Left out: object files, built binaries, and the *-orig.c /
*-old.c backup copies. No upstream history kept.

Build each part with "make -f GNUmakefile" in CPP, CC09, COpt and DCC.
harness/dccdiff.py compares this build with CoCoC's on every C source.

Changes (phase 6, docs/DESIGN.md D18):
  CC09  identifiers significant to 31 characters (NAMESIZE, was 8); symbol
        entries keep room for 8 and grow only for longer names; full names
        in the assembly; fixed: getword's buffer overflow, settype leaving
        the dimension list unset and an unterminated dimension chain
        (crash on XLisp/xlkmap.c)
  COpt  labels up to 32 characters (LABELSIZE, was 11); fixed: "puls u"
        read two bytes before its operand
  DCC   runs las instead of rma

Changes (phase 7, native build; docs/DESIGN.md D20, D25):
  CC09  on OS-9, allocates with sbrk instead of ibrk (cj.h ALLOCATE), so
        dcc68 can start with a small data area and grow: the F256 won't
        fork a 6-block module with more than 8K of initial data
  COpt  "#define void int" on OS-9 (op.h): DCC itself has no void
Changes (phase 10; docs/DESIGN.md D33):
  CC09  a char function's result used as a condition (if (f()), while,
        ?:) is tested with tstb, not "std -2,s": the callee sets only B
        (bool.c checkop). Inherited from CoCoC; dccdiff unchanged
Changes (2026-10-07; docs/DESIGN.md D39; also made in the CoCoC tree):
  DCC   -w no longer passes -n to dcc68, which never accepted it ("unknown
        flag: -n"); on Linux runit passes each pass's exit code back
        (exit(system()) made every failure 0)
Changes (2026-10-08; docs/DESIGN.md D42):
  DCC   runs llink (our rlink fork, renamed) instead of rlink, so it never
        picks up the original rlink from PATH or /dd/CMDS
Changes (2026-10-09, step 14; docs/DESIGN.md D43):
  CC09  a result in X (long, float, double) with 2 bytes to pop: "puls d",
        not "leas 2,s" (xmodstk, codgen.c; doreturn, tranexp), since dco68
        turns "leas 2,s / puls u,pc" into "puls x,u,pc"; room for it from
        storerr/ptrmis/indir (misc.c), one copy of three repeated messages
  COpt  level1.patterns: "puls d / puls u,pc" -> "puls d,u,pc"; the Linux
        build reads its patterns from this directory, not ~/.dcc
Changes (2026-10-13, step 17: header images; docs/DESIGN.md D50):
  CC09  -h=IMAGE: when lookup() makes a new symbol, pch.c loads its
        declaration from a header image if the image has the name (a
        filter in memory, then hash chains on disk); names a file never
        uses are never loaded. Built with -DMKIMG it is dcc68w, which
        writes an image (-w=IMAGE) of a headers-only file; native, it is
        the parser alone (nogen.c stands in for the rest), 4 blocks
  CC09  messages: each is a 2-byte code (msgs.h, where the texts are
        comments); msg() reads its text from /dd/SYS/dcc68.msg (on Linux
        CC09/dcc68.msg, made from msgs.h), so the texts cost no room
  CPP   -h=IMAGE: headers the image holds are read (their #defines count)
        but not passed on; each one's text must have the image's checksum,
        else dcpp exits 2. Headers the image doesn't hold pass as usual
  DCC   -H=IMAGE FILE.c makes an image (dcpp, dcc68w); -h=IMAGE uses one,
        and compiles a file without it when dcpp exits 2, saying so

Changes (2026-10-13, step 18: float constants; docs/DESIGN.md D52):
  CC09  on Linux a float or double constant is kept in the 6809's format
        (DBLETYPE is a struct there) and built, negated and converted the
        way the 6809's cfloats.a does it (fp6809.c, which replaces
        fltconv.c's IEEE conversion; scale.c is the 6809's only); the
        constant operations in optim.c, inits.c go through cj.h's D_
        macros, which on the 6809 are the plain C they were
  CC09  6809 fixes: normaliz() adds the digit sum's low word as unsigned
        (4294967295.0 was 3865470565); scale() leaves zero alone (0.0 was
        2^126); a decimal constant 32768..65535 is a long (65535 was the
        int -1). On Linux addin() overflows at 2^56, as on the 6809

The 6809 build (../native/GNUmakefile) compiles dcc68 with -s and
without -DPROF so it stays at most 48,384 bytes (6 blocks ending by $FD00);
it is 48,381 now.
Design and roadmap: ../docs/DESIGN.md
